config REKERNELX
	bool "ReKernel-X"
	depends on KSU
	help
	  ReKernel-X surfaces kernel-side events for frozen (cached) processes so
	  tombstone-style modules can react to them:
	    - Binder: a frozen process receiving a Binder call
	    - Signal: a frozen process receiving SIGKILL and friends
	    - Network: a monitored UID receiving an inbound packet

	  Events are delivered to userspace over Generic Netlink. The hooks are
	  resolved at runtime through kprobes, so the module does not need
	  compile-time access to the binder internals and builds against both
	  4.14 and 5.10+ trees.

	  Say N if unsure.